The technique I used was to make sure I had some protection from level
drain (depending on alignment.  magic resistance or mithril armor if
neutral) and I stayed on the stairs.  If I got too low on hp, I'd run
up the stairs, bringing a couple undead up with me.  I could kill those
and then rest.  Or, if even that's too tough, you could wait to be 
surrounded, then go upstairs, kill those ~7 undead, then go down, get
7 more, and keep doing that.  But use the stairs, trust me!  Also, if
you get drained, make sure you only get drained one level.  If you get
drained one, the next kill will put you back.  But if you get two, you
can't get the first one back easily.

